WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.330
A man steals mangoes from
his neighbour's tree.

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.440
When he is caught, he
has a clever defence.

3
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.440
These are not the mangoes
you planted, he says.

4
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:10.990
You planted seeds.

5
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.050
These are different fruit.

6
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.450
An old Buddhist text tells
this story for a reason.

7
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.610
Buddhists teach anatta: there
is no fixed, unchanging self.

8
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.700
So if there is no fixed
self, who chooses to act,

9
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.720
and who is to blame?

10
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:33.140
In this mission, you'll learn how Buddhists
sort actions into kusala and akusala:

11
00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.150
healthy and unhealthy.

12
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.050
Then you'll meet a modern scholar who
compares Buddhist ethics with virtue ethics.

13
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.950
Your mission: find out what
makes an action good or bad,

14
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.400
and who answers for it.
